"K'ssk Swamp"
"The moist, black soils of the swamp are dominated by a variety of woody

plants, including a small stand of cypress trees and a couple of hibiscus

bushes.  Two sturdy animal trails meander through the marshy land, snaking

through the underbrush from north to south like a water moccasin through a

stream.  The plants and soil here are relatively undisturbed; there is little

sign of any faunal activity.  To the east is a small running stream that

courses north to south.

